I think I found another bug by making the test.

On SSR there an error when the value passed to `{#each}` si nullable, in [ensure_array_like()](https://github.com/sveltejs/svelte/blob/6776947ae85e58a2a947d1ce3143b4af3f799466/packages/svelte/src/internal/server/index.js#L509) :
```js
/** @param {any} array_like_or_iterator */
export function ensure_array_like(array_like_or_iterator) {
	return array_like_or_iterator?.length !== undefined
		? array_like_or_iterator
		: Array.from(array_like_or_iterator);
}
```

When `array_like_or_iterator` is a null/undefined, this will call `Array.from()` with an invalid value.


It should be : 
```js
/** @param {any} array_like_or_iterator */
export function ensure_array_like(array_like_or_iterator) {
	if (array_like_or_iterator) {
		return array_like_or_iterator.length !== undefined
			? array_like_or_iterator
			: Array.from(array_like_or_iterator);
	}
	return [];
}
```

